---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
import { languages, disclosure } from '../lib/resume';
import Chronology from '../components/Chronology.astro';
---

<Base title="About — Amrullah Amiri">
  <section class="editorial pt-16">
    <h1 class="display text-4xl">About</h1>
    <span class="rule-draw mt-8" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial pt-10 pb-8">
    <div class="measure space-y-5 lg:row-1">
      <p>
        I&rsquo;m a {site.role.toLowerCase()} at {site.school} in {site.location}, finishing
        in {site.graduates}. I&rsquo;m heading toward {site.focus}, and I came to all of
        it late.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before this I spent about a decade doing other work. I grew up in Afghanistan and
        worked in Kabul and Kandahar &mdash; a call center, then supervising accounts for
        a trading group. I spent two years as a linguist with Mission Essential in Bagram.
        After I came to California I interpreted Pashto and English over the phone for
        hospitals, courts and 911 dispatchers, which is a strange and clarifying job: you
        are the only reason two people in a room can understand each other, and you get
        no second take.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then I did accounting. Two years owning month-end close at a company in Lafayette
        &mdash; AP and AR, reconciliations, the general ledger, the audit trail. That is
        where I met the software I now write. Most of it was bad in a specific way: it
        was built by people who had never had to close a month with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        So that&rsquo;s the thing I&rsquo;m actually for. I like problems where a number
        has to be right, where somebody downstream is depending on it, and where the
        boring path &mdash; validation, an audit trail, a test &mdash; is the interesting
        one. My best project is a reporting system for gas stations, which sounds like
        nothing until you have been the person reconciling the paperwork.
      </p>
      <p>
        I speak three languages and I have been the person on the wrong side of a
        language barrier, which is most of why machine learning interests me at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        I finish my associate&rsquo;s at Los Medanos in December 2026 and transfer to
        San&nbsp;José State for the B.S. in Spring 2027.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="col-side mt-10 border-t border-rule pt-5 lg:row-1 lg:mt-0 lg:border-0 lg:pt-0">
      <h2 class="label">Now</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm text-muted">
        {site.now.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2 class="label mt-10">Languages</h2>
      <dl class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
        {
          languages.map((lang) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="inline text-ink-soft">{lang.name}</dt>
              <dd class="inline text-muted"> &mdash; {lang.level}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial pb-8">
    <div class="col-wide mt-8">
      <h2 class="label">Chronology</h2>
      <p class="measure mt-3 text-muted italic">
        Eleven jobs, four cities, three languages, one degree in progress.
      </p>
      <Chronology />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="editorial pb-8">
    <div class="measure mt-8 border-t border-rule pt-8">
      <h2 class="label">How these were built</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
        {disclosure.split('\n\n').map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
